  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe proposed strategy employs a convex optimization framework with a novel dual ascent mechanism to address the non-convex nature of the overlap maximization. By introducing dual variables for each lag and leveraging the structure of the problem, we systematically minimize the maximum overlap while maintaining feasibility.\n\nThe key innovation is the use of a variational inference approach to update dual variables, allowing us to handle the maximum operation in a distributed manner. This approach avoids getting trapped in local optima and provides a more directed search compared to simulated annealing.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nWe introduce dual variables \u03bb_k for each lag k \u2208 [-n_points+1, n_points-1], with:\n- \u03bb_k \u2265 0\n- sum(\u03bb_k) = 1\n\nThe Lagrangian is:\nL(h, \u03bb) = sum(\u03bb_k * overlap_k) + \u03b7*(sum(h) - n_points/2)\n\nwhere overlap_k = \u222b h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx, and \u03b7 is the multiplier enforcing the sum constraint.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na) Initialization:\n   - Set n_points = 100, dx = 2.0 / n_points\n   - Initialize h from initial_h_values or randomly\n   - Clip and scale h to satisfy constraints\n\nb) Main loop:\n   For each iteration until budget exhausted:\n      i) Compute all overlap_k via convolution\n      ii) Update \u03bb_k using variational inference to focus on dominant overlaps\n      iii) Compute gradients \u2202L/\u2202h[i] for each i\n      iv) Update h using gradient descent with learning rate\n      v) Repair h to maintain constraints\n      vi) Track best solution\n\nc) Dual variable update:\n   \u03bb_k \u221d exp(-overlap_k / \u03c4), where \u03c4 is a temperature parameter\n\nd) Gradient computation:\n   For each i, \u2202L/\u2202h[i] = sum(\u03bb_k * (1 - h[i - k] if k \u2264 i else 0))\n\ne) Repair mechanism:\n   1. Clip h to [0,1]\n   2. Scale h to ensure sum(h) = n_points / 2\n\nf) Termination:\n   - Stop on budget exhaustion or no improvement for N iterations\n   - Return best solution with verified C\u2085\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Initial h: Use initial_h_values or Poisson spike distribution\n- Learning rate: Start at 5e-4, decrease by 0.99 every 500 steps\n- Temperature \u03c4: Start at 0.1, decrease by 0.999 per iteration\n- Dual update frequency: Every 10 gradient steps\n- Fallback to initial_h_values on stagnation\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Each dual ascent cycle with gradient steps takes ~20ms\n- Expect ~30000 iterations in 600s\n- Robust to stagnation via dual variable adaptation\n- Safe fallback to initial_h_values\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Verify sum(h) equals n_points / 2 within 1e-8\n- Validate all h[i] \u2208 [0,1]\n- Recompute C\u2085 via evaluate_h to confirm\n- Ensure no NaNs or infs in h or C\u2085",
